# netsurf: any sheet, removal or root change during a load is walked against the live cascade (patch 455)
# Generated 2026-11-26
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 454)
#
# "sheet change: a sheet is still loading or changing" (2.3 a load in the
# 454 census: google, bbc, oldreddit) declined into the full rebuild unless
# 443's no-walk answer applied (nothing pruned, the tree holding the
# context's generation). But a full rebuild during a load cascades the live
# c->select_ctx as it is (it is refreshed only once every sheet settled),
# and html_rl_doc_noop's walk compares EVERY element's box against the
# context it is given: so walking against the live context, its hits
# restyled in place (447/451), is exactly that rebuild's result whatever
# generation the tree holds. 453 did this for a removal when the tree held
# the context's generation; 455 drops that condition (html_rl_removal_held
# goes) and takes any change -- sheet change, removal, root -- unless a
# sheet's text update is pending (its rules are in no context yet). 443's
# answer stays first: it needs no walk. 442's NET-js-sheet-wait is now
# answered at once instead of waiting.
#
--- a/content/handlers/html/html.c
+++ b/content/handlers/html/html.c
@@ -9053,11 +9053,6 @@
